* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* RUN of a class module, or a catalogue reference to one, as a command.  kernel.c k_call() finds that what it has been asked
* to run is a CLASS and, when the request came from RUN or a command (op_run, op_chain), runs this subroutine instead with the
* name it was given: a catalogue name, or the pathname of a runfile.  OBJECT() makes the object, which runs the CREATE.OBJECT
* subroutine if the class has one; the MAIN subroutine is the class's main program; when this subroutine returns the object is
* let go and its DESTROY.OBJECT subroutine runs.  A class with no MAIN gets the run time's usual message for a name an object
* does not have: 'Unrecognised property/method name (MAIN)'.  A CALL of a class is still refused (message 3450).
*
* An internal program may name a runfile by its pathname in OBJECT() (objprog.c, op_object).
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
$no.symbols
$no.xref

subroutine $classmain(class.name)
$catalog $CLASSMAIN

   o = object(class.name)
   o->main
   return
end

* END-CODE
